{"id": "xturkmen", "name": "Repetek Biosphere Reserve", "short": "Repetek", "place": "Turkmenistan", "lat": 38.6, "lon": 63.2, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Turkmenistan", "kind": "Desert", "park": true, "blurb": "Saxaul sand desert where gerbils, lizards and a big monitor share scarce water.", "tip": {"id": "gerbil", "title": "Remove the great gerbil", "text": "Gerbils feed owls, snakes, foxes and the desert monitor. Set Great gerbil to -100% and watch the predators that rely on it."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Repetek Nature Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Repetek_Nature_Reserve"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Karakum Desert", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karakum_Desert"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Haloxylon ammodendron", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haloxylon_ammodendron"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Desert monitor", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_monitor"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Caspian cobra", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caspian_cobra"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Great grey shrike", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_grey_shrike"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Repetek Nature Reserve", "icon": "sage", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Intense desert sun drives plant growth but also the summer heat and drought that limit it."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "scarce rainfall", "xh": 0.32, "wiki": "Desert climate", "desc": "The Karakum gets only about 70 to 150 mm of rain a year, so a short spring flush of annual plants matters a great deal."}, {"id": "sand", "sp": "sandy soil and dunes", "xh": 0.56}, {"id": "groundwater", "sp": "groundwater", "xh": 0.78, "latin": "", "name": "Groundwater", "desc": "Deep-rooted desert shrubs tap water below the sand surface, which lets them survive long dry spells. General ecology.", "ic": "water"}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.92, "name": "Soil microbes and fungi", "desc": "Soil algae, fungi and bacteria break down dead plants and animals and return nutrients to the sand."}, {"id": "blacksaxaul", "sp": "haloxylon ammodendron", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "A leafless desert tree of sandy deserts that forms saxaul woodland in Central Asia and is the signature plant of the reserve. Locusts and beetles attack it.", "ic": "sage"}, {"id": "whitesaxaul", "sp": "haloxylon persicum", "xh": 0.38}, {"id": "calligonum", "sp": "calligonum", "xh": 0.62}, {"id": "ephemerals", "sp": "schismus arabicus", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "gazelle", "sp": "gazella subgutturosa", "xh": 0.06, "desc": "A vulnerable desert antelope of sands and gravel plains, with a significant population in the reserve. Herds travel to find food."}, {"id": "gerbil", "sp": "rhombomys opimus", "xh": 0.2}, {"id": "locust", "sp": "dericorys", "xh": 0.34}, {"id": "beetles", "sp": "tenebrionidae", "xh": 0.49}, {"id": "sparrow", "sp": "passer ammodendri", "xh": 0.65}, {"id": "gecko", "sp": "teratoscincus scincus", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "agama", "sp": "trapelus sanguinolentus", "xh": 0.2}, {"id": "racer", "sp": "psammophis lineolatus", "xh": 0.36}, {"id": "groundjay", "sp": "podoces panderi", "xh": 0.52}, {"id": "shrike", "sp": "lanius excubitor", "xh": 0.68, "desc": "A songbird predator that takes large insects, small rodents, lizards and small birds, and impales surplus prey on thorns."}, {"id": "owl", "sp": "athene noctua", "xh": 0.85, "desc": "A small owl that eats insects and small vertebrates, including mammals, reptiles and birds."}, {"id": "monitor", "sp": "varanus griseus", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "A large burrowing lizard that eats mammals, reptiles, birds, eggs and insects, and also feeds on carrion. The reserve is known for it.", "badge": "Keystone predator"}, {"id": "cobra", "sp": "